-- string-zero/divergence --
suite: emit-probes
case: string-zero.tck
go: Go pools the empty string only where its walk sees a string start from
  its zero value, so the zero value of a checked pop, remove, delete or
  pool remove of strings gets an empty label, (tack_string){,
  TACK_C_STR_LEN()}, and a pool[string]'s take helper names the pooled
  empty string before the pool declares it: neither compiles.
why: The port pools the empty string after the walk when a zero value needs
  it, and the take helper leaves a zeroed string in the slot, under the
  lead's ruling of 2026-11-15 that the language already defines the zero
  values, which the language owner may overrule. The C compiles and runs
  under the address, undefined behavior and leak sanitizers with clang
  -Wall -Werror.
same: none
-- string-zero/exit --
0
